0	section	Return to Ardougne
0	section	Talking to Elena after talking to Guidor
1	line	Elena	You're back! So what did Guidor say?
1	line	Player	Nothing.
1	line	Elena	What?
1	line	Player	He ran his tests and discovered nothing. The plague... it doesn't exist.
1	line	Elena	Doesn't exist? But I don't understand... why?
1	line	Player	I don't know, but I think we're about to uncover something huge.
1	line	Elena	Well I think there's only one thing for it. The king must be confronted!
1	line	Player	The king?
1	line	Elena	Yes. King Lathas of East Ardougne. He was the one that had the wall built. He was the one who called the mourners in. He must know what's really going on here.
1	line	Player	Well I'd better go and speak to the king then.
1	line	Elena	Be quick. You should find him in the castle.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Elena again before talking to the King
1	line	Player	Hello Elena.
1	line	Elena	You must go and see King Lathas immediately!
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to King Lathas after talking to Elena about the plague
1	line	Player	I assume that you are King Lathas of East Ardougne?
1	line	King Lathas	You assume correctly, but where do you get such impertinence.
1	line	Player	I get it from finding out that the plague is a hoax.
1	line	King Lathas	A hoax? I've never heard such a ridiculous thing...
1	line	Player	I have evidence, from Guidor of Varrock.
1	line	King Lathas	Ah... I see. Well then you are right about the plague. But I did it for the good of my people.
1	line	Player	When is it ever good to lie to people like that?
1	line	King Lathas	When it protects them from a far greater danger, a fear too big to fathom.
1	line	Player	I don't understand...
1	line	King Lathas	When my father was king, he ruled over a united Ardougne. But on his deathbed, he could not decide which of his sons should succeed him, so he had the city split into two.
1	line	King Lathas	I became king of East Ardougne while my brother, Tyras, ruled over West Ardougne. My brother was a good man and was great at many things. Being a king was not one of them.
1	line	King Lathas	Rather than looking after his people, he went on numerous expeditions to the lands west of here. On one of these expeditions, he was captured by the forces of the Dark Lord.
1	line	King Lathas	The Dark Lord agreed to spare his life, but only on one condition... That he would drink from the Chalice of Eternity.
1	line	Player	So what happened?
1	line	King Lathas	The chalice corrupted him. He joined forces with the Dark Lord, the embodiment of pure evil...
1	line	King Lathas	And so I erected the wall, not just to protect my people, but to protect all the people of Gielinor. Tyras is king of West Ardougne, sealing off the city was the only way to stop him and the Dark Lord.
1	line	King Lathas	I knew people would never believe the truth, so I had the plague made up as an excuse for the cordon. I'm not proud of it, but it was the only way to keep people safe.
1	line	Player	I see. Well at least I know now.
1	line	King Lathas	While my brother is still at large, I must ask that you keep this secret. We can't bring the wall down until we know he is no longer a danger.
1	line	Player	But how do we stop him?
1	line	King Lathas	You're willing to help? Gods be praised!
1	line	King Lathas	My brother is currently gathering strength in the lands to the west. If we are to stop him, we must find a way through the mountains. There is an underground pass that should lead through but it is full of danger.
1	line	King Lathas	Return to me when you are ready to face this peril. Until then, I give you permission to use my training area. It's located just to the north west of the city.
1	line	King Lathas	I'll also let the mourners know that you are a friend to Ardougne. You will be allowed to pass through the gates to West Ardougne whenever you please. Now, you'd better be off. You have much to prepare for.
1	line	King Lathas	Do you need anything else adventurer?
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	Why don't I get started right away?
2	line	Player	Why don't I get started right away?
2	line	King Lathas	Your enthusiasm is to be commended. Very well, if you feel you are already prepared then who am I to stop you.
2	line	King Lathas	As we've previously discussed, my brother is currently gathering strength in the lands west of here. The only known way into those lands is through the Underground Pass.
2	action	(Continues with Underground Pass dialogue.)
1	option	I don't think so.
2	line	Player	I don't think so.
2	line	King Lathas	Very well. Return to me once you are ready and we will discuss our next steps.
2	action	end
